    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor differences in phrasing of problem summaries, or not hitting exactly 5 results when fewer exist (if explained) would be nitpicks.\n\nCritical issues:\n1) Missing required searches/coverage: Evidence shows global searches for \u201cerror\u201d and \u201cissue\u201d (e.g., \u201cResults for: error\u201d across many screenshots; \u201cResults for: issue\u201d in screenshots 25-26). There is no evidence the agent searched \u201cfailed\u201d or \u201chelp,\u201d and the predicted output only summarizes a single \u201cissue\u201d item.\n2) Missing primary deliverable (final table): The task\u2019s main output is a deduplicated table with columns (term, channel, author, timestamp, problem summary, latest visible response, status). The agent produced no table\u2014only a narrative for one thread and even states it\u2019s \u201cready to be placed into the final\u2026 table later,\u201d meaning the deliverable was not produced.\n3) No deduplication: With only one row of narrative output and no consolidated multi-term results, there is no deduplication across searches.\n4) Likely fabrication/unsupported details: The predicted output claims specific timestamps and multiple thread replies (e.g., Nikola \u201cInvestigating\u201d at 3:09 AM; \u201cThanks, it\u2019s working now!\u201d; closing the thread). In the \u201cissue\u201d screenshot evidence (25-26), the UI shows the Aug 20 item exists and indicates a thread (\u201c1 reply\u201d in screenshot 26 / \u201c4 replies\u201d in screenshot 25), but the reply texts themselves are not visible in the provided screenshots. Since screenshots are ground truth for verification here, the agent\u2019s detailed reply content and the \u201cexplicitly resolved\u201d determination are not supported by visible evidence.\n\nWhat the agent did accomplish: It did substantial inspection of several \u201cerror\u201d results and clearly consulted thread panels there (screenshots 7, 11, 13, 15), and it did run an \u201cissue\u201d search by the end (screenshots 25-26). It also did not modify Slack content.\n\nOutcome vs. task: Despite some correct navigation and thread-reading for \u201cerror,\u201d the agent did not complete the required four searches, did not produce the required final deduplicated table, and the single reported row contains reply/resolution details not corroborated by the visible evidence set. An average user would consider the task incomplete and unreliable.",
